Why the split: the engine is a service you run, so AGPL applies — modify it
and offer it to others as a service, and your modifications must be published.
The specification, corpora, SDKs and builder frontends are things developers
link into their own code, so they are permissive: a copyleft client SDK would
be unusable, and an encumbered specification would not be a specification.

